    {
      "title": "Why hexadecimal is used",
      "objectives": [
        "12.1.1.2"
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "cards",
          "items": [
            {
              "title": "Advantages of hexadecimal",
              "content": "- **Shorter** than binary — a byte is **2** hex digits instead of **8** bits.\n- **Easier for people to read, remember and write** → **fewer mistakes** when copying long binary values.\n- **Easy and quick to convert** to and from binary (each digit = 4 bits) — much easier than denary.\n- Makes **debugging** and low-level programming quicker."
            },
            {
              "title": "What hex does NOT do",
              "content": "- It does **not save memory** — the computer still stores everything in **binary**.\n- It does **not make the computer faster**. Hex is only a **representation for humans**."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "comparison",
          "title": "Uses of hexadecimal",
          "columns": [
            "Use",
            "Example",
            "Why hex"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "**Colour codes** (24-bit RGB)",
              "`#1F4FD8` = red 1F (31), green 4F (79), blue D8 (216)",
              "6 digits instead of 24 bits"
            ],
            [
              "**Memory addresses**",
              "`0x7FFE4A10` in debuggers and error messages",
              "Long addresses become short"
            ],
            [
              "**MAC addresses**",
              "`3C:52:82:1A:9F:04`",
              "48 bits → 12 hex digits"
            ],
            [
              "**Machine code / memory dumps**",
              "`B8 04 00 CD 21`",
              "Each byte = 2 digits"
            ],
            [
              "**Error and status codes**",
              "Windows `0x80070005`",
              "Compact, matches binary flags"
            ],
            [
              "**IPv6 addresses**",
              "`2001:0db8::1`",
              "128 bits → 32 hex digits"
            ],
            [
              "**Character codes**",
              "Unicode `U+04D8` (Ә)",
              "Code points are listed in hex"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "example",
          "title": "Colour code in binary and hex",
          "content": "Pure orange **#FF8000**: red = FF = 11111111, green = 80 = 10000000, blue = 00 = 00000000. Writing **24 bits** by hand (111111111000000000000000) is slow and error-prone; **6 hex digits** are quick to read and type."
        }
      ]
    },
